<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iberian Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1580">1580</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Iberian Union was the dynastic union of the crowns of Portugal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> under the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> kings, beginning in 1580 and lasting until 1640. Portugal kept its own institutions but was drawn into Spain's wars. Its overseas possessions were attacked by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and English, a significant phase in the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iberian-union.jpg" alt="Iberian Union" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gabriel Ziegler · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IberianUnionandCouncils.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Iberian Union</b> of 1580, while preserving Portuguese laws and institutions, exposed Portugal’s overseas empire to the consequences of Spain’s wars: the Dutch, in revolt against Spain, became systematic rivals who penetrated Portuguese Asian trade networks with devastating effectiveness, capturing Malacca in 1641 and Ceylon in stages between…</blockquote><a href="/empire/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Their victory at Alcácer Quibir had consequences far beyond Morocco: the death of the childless Sebastian led to a succession crisis that ended with Philip II of Spain taking the Portuguese crown in 1580, beginning the <b>Iberian Union</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/saadi-sultanate">Saadi Sultanate · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
